nvites-north-for-military-talks-over-border?traffic_source=rss","p":"Al Jazeera English","d":"2026-10-23T10:20:31Z","o":false,"dup":false}],"related":[],"revisions":[{"revision":1,"changed_at":"2026-10-24T11:00:49Z"}],"entities":[{"name":"South Korea","kind":"place","mentions":2},{"name":"North","kind":"place","mentions":1},{"name":"North Korea","kind":"place","mentions":1},{"name":"Pyongyang","kind":"place","mentions":1}],"disputes":[],"summary":null,"context":{"background":[],"places":[{"title":"South Korea","extract":"South Korea, officially the Republic of Korea (ROK), is a country in East Asia. It constitutes the southern half of the Korean Peninsula and borders North Korea along the Korean Demilitarized Zone, with the Yellow Sea to the west and the Sea of Japan to the east. South Korea claims to be the sole legitimate government of the entire peninsula and adjacent islands. It has a population of about 52 million, of which half live in the Seoul metropolitan area, the ninth most populous metropolitan area in the world, with other major cities being Busan, Daegu, and Incheon.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Korea","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"KR"},{"title":"North Korea","extract":"North Korea, officially the Democratic People's Republic of Korea (DPRK), is a country in East Asia. It constitutes the northern half of the Korean Peninsula and borders China and Russia to the north at the Yalu (Amnok) and Tumen rivers, and South Korea to the south at the Korean Demilitarized Zone (DMZ). The country's western border is formed by the Yellow Sea, while its eastern border is defined by the Sea of Japan. Pyongyang is the capital and largest city.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Korea","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"KP"}],"arc":{"reports":11,"first_seen":"2026-10-10T18:14:33Z","first_title":"South Korea Launches First Hypersonic Glide Vehicle Five Years Behind the North","first_url":"https://news.goog